    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d564">

                <pb facs="0636" n="624" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg624"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24532/18</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Under
                        Secretary of War</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Patterson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-03-29">March 29, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I enclose for your
                    information a copy of despatch no. 159 of February 24, 1943,<anchor n="20"
                        xml:id="d564-f1"/> received in this Department from the American Consul at
                    Para, Brazil recommending the withdrawal of the United States Army detachment at
                    Manáos, Brazil. There are also enclosed paraphrases of telegrams<anchor n="20"
                        xml:id="d564-f2"/> exchanged between the Department of State and the
                    American Ambassador at Bio de Janeiro on this subject.</p>
                <p>In the light of the comment made by Ambassador Caffery in his telegram no. 1438,
                    March 23,<anchor n="21" xml:id="d564-f3"/> concerning the continued presence in
                    Manáos of this Army detachment, I believe that you may wish to investigate the
                    desirability of assigning this unit to other duty. I should appreciate being
                    informed of any action taken by the War Department in this regard.</p>
                <p>Believe me,</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d564-f1" n="20" xml:id="d564-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d564-f2" n="20" xml:id="d564-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d564-f3" n="21" xml:id="d564-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed; the Ambassador recommended that the air forces remain one more month
                    in Manáos, and he reported the rise of some resentment among Brazilians at the
                    continued presence of the Americans.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
